{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "The eight relations charts from the live Prometheus/Mimir with the transformation chain deleted: plain ranged `topk(sum by (client, server) (…))` queries and an empty Transform tab on seven of eight panels, reshaped by the plugin's registered longToWide pivot instead of instant + label_join + organize + rowsToFields. Keeps the row dimension, so Reduce is a real choice. The reader accepts conventional endpoint pairs, so the service-graph panels need neither `label_replace` nor a filter-label config; the two whose levels relabel from cluster/namespace still do. Node stats still need rowsToFields (panel 4). Sibling of echarts-relations-devcortex, deliberately on the same variables and layout.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "The instant route this replaces",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/echarts-relations-devcortex",
      "icon": "external link",
      "tags": [],
      "targetBlank": false,
      "asDropdown": false,
      "includeVars": true,
      "keepTime": true
    }
  ],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 18,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Live Prometheus range queries\n\nSeven panels use Prometheus range queries without dashboard transformations. The plugin converts each labeled series into an edge field before field overrides run.\n\nThis conversion requires Grafana 13.2 or later and the `grafana.panelPluginTransformations` feature toggle. It recognizes `source`/`target`, `client`/`server`, `src`/`dst`, and `from`/`to` label pairs.\n\nCalculation reduces each edge series across the selected time range. The node-value query in panel 4 still uses Organize fields and Rows to fields."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The variables",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Variables and filters\n\nAll query variables support multiple values. The All value is `.*`, so Prometheus matchers use `=~`.\n\n`$cluster`, `$namespace`, `$client`, and `$server` filter service traffic. `$connection` filters connection types. `$topk` limits edges.\n\nSelect a node or edge to pin its tooltip. If the field is Filterable, the footer can add or exclude values through the `$filters` variable.\n\nExternal services can have no server Kubernetes labels. Server-scoped panels can omit those services."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Prometheus — the queries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 29
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Panels 1 to 4\n\nThe service map uses a range query with `client` and `server` labels. Last shows the newest request rate.\n\nThe CPU Sankey copies cluster, namespace, and workload values into endpoint labels. Mean shows the average over the time range.\n\nThe service Chord filters both endpoints to the selected namespace.\n\nPanel 4 adds a node-value query for the service error ratio. That node query uses Organize fields and Rows to fields."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "Service dependency map — graph",
      "description": "Shows the top `$topk` service calls from a Prometheus range query. Last shows the newest request rate. Dashboard variables filter the client side.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prom}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 0,
          "filterable": true
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "seriesType": "graph",
        "editorMode": "advanced",
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        },
        "relationsFocusAdjacency": true,
        "relationsLayout": "circular",
        "relationsEdgeArrows": true,
        "relationsNodeSize": 18,
        "relationsCurveness": 0.1,
        "relationsLinkColor": "source",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prom}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "topk($topk,\n  sum by (client, server) (\n    rate(traces_service_graph_request_total{client_k8s_cluster_name=~\"$cluster\", client_k8s_namespace_name=~\"$namespace\", client=~\"$client\", server=~\"$server\", client!=\"\", server!=\"\"}[$__range])\n  )\n)",
          "exemplar": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "__auto"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "CPU requests: cluster → namespace → workload — sankey",
      "description": "Shows requested CPU from cluster to namespace to workload. Mean shows the average over the selected time range.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prom}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "unit": "suffix:cores",
          "decimals": 1,
          "filterable": true
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "seriesType": "sankey",
        "editorMode": "advanced",
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        },
        "relationsFocusAdjacency": true,
        "relationsSankeyOrient": "horizontal",
        "relationsSankeyNodeAlign": "justify",
        "relationsSankeyNodeWidth": 18,
        "relationsSankeyNodeGap": 10,
        "relationsSankeyLinkOpacity": 0.45,
        "relationsShowNodeValues": false,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["mean"]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prom}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (source, target, cluster, namespace) (\n  label_replace(\n    label_replace(\n      topk($topk,\n        sum by (cluster, namespace) (\n          kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource=\"cpu\", cluster=~\"$cluster\", namespace=~\"$namespace\", cluster!=\"\", namespace!=\"\"}\n        )\n      ),\n      \"source\", \"$1\", \"cluster\", \"(.*)\"\n    ),\n    \"target\", \"$1\", \"namespace\", \"(.*)\"\n  )\n)\n  or\nsum by (source, target, namespace, workload) (\n  label_replace(\n    label_replace(\n      topk($topk,\n        sum by (namespace, workload) (\n          namespace_workload_pod:kube_pod_owner:relabel{namespace=~\"$namespace\"}\n            * on (namespace, pod) group_left()\n              sum by (namespace, pod) (\n                kube_pod_container_resource_requests{resource=\"cpu\", cluster=~\"$cluster\", namespace=~\"$namespace\"}\n              )\n        )\n      ),\n      \"source\", \"$1\", \"namespace\", \"(.*)\"\n    ),\n    \"target\", \"$1\", \"workload\", \"(.*)\"\n  )\n)",
          "exemplar": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "instant": false,
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "__auto"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": []
    },
    {
